WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.100
Why a runbook?

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.713
Because each earlier lab proves
one provider on its own,

3
00:00:04.713 --> 00:00:09.112
and production needs all of them
together, every week, with a way back.

4
00:00:09.112 --> 00:00:10.763
So the goal is concrete.

5
00:00:10.763 --> 00:00:15.184
By the end you can deploy the kit to a
test environment and then to production,

6
00:00:15.184 --> 00:00:17.851
with a change record, an
approval at each write,

7
00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:22.343
a smoke test whose expected result is
written down before you run it, evidence

8
00:00:22.343 --> 00:00:26.625
the security officer can check with a
hash, and a rollback you've rehearsed.

9
00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:31.150
And for every step you can say which of
the guide's seven gates it moves forward.
